---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Econometrics from '../../layouts/Econometrics.astro';
import Worlds from '../../components/econometrics/Worlds.astro';
import {chapterTopics} from '../../data/econometrics.mjs';
import '../../styles/measurement.css';
const chapters=(await getCollection('econometrics')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
const spine=[['Target','What would the answer mean?'],['Observe','Who enters the data?'],['Identify','Which rival worlds remain?'],['Estimate','What does the procedure recover?'],['Quantify','How could this answer fail?'],['Decide','What action survives the uncertainty?']];
---
<Econometrics>
  <section class="ea-shell ea-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="ea-kicker">An open course in econometrics · Ian Helfrich</p>
      <h1>The Econometric<br/>Argument</h1>
      <p class="ea-lead">An introduction to econometrics: probability, regression, causal identification, and decisions under uncertainty.</p>

      <div class="ea-actions"><a class="ea-button" href="/econometrics/01-argument/">Open the first chapter <span>→</span></a><a class="ea-button secondary" href="#contents">Contents</a></div>
      <p class="ea-small">12 compact chapters · 3 experiments · worked problems<br/>Development edition, September 2026</p>
    </div>
    <Worlds compact />
  </section>
  <section class="ea-shell m-feature"><div class="m-feature-inner"><div><small>Measurement: essay, exercises, and theory</small><h2>What did the number leave out?</h2></div><div><p>Compare two service designs: one offers faster appointments, the other gives participants more control. The ranking depends on how both outcomes are measured and weighted.</p><a href="/econometrics/measurement/">Open the measurement investigation</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="ea-shell ea-band">
    <div class="ea-split"><h2>Does training improve productivity?</h2><div><p>Workers who take more training produce more. Training may improve productivity, or more productive workers may be more likely to enroll.</p><p>The chapters use this example to study selection, estimation, and the evidence needed to justify expanding a training program.</p></div></div>
    <ol class="ea-spine">{spine.map(([label,detail])=><li><strong>{label}</strong><span>{detail}</span></li>)}</ol>
  </section>
  <section class="ea-shell ea-band" id="contents" data-course-index>
    <div class="ea-contents-head"><div><p class="ea-kicker">The book</p><h2>Contents</h2></div><div><p class="ea-small" data-course-progress>Reading progress is optional and stays on this device.</p><a class="ea-small" href="/econometrics/print/">Open the printable edition →</a></div></div>
    <div class="ea-route-picks" role="group" aria-label="Choose a suggested reading path"><button data-path="all" aria-pressed="true">The full argument</button><button data-path="first" aria-pressed="false">My first course</button><button data-path="applied" aria-pressed="false">I work with data</button><button data-path="theory" aria-pressed="false">Take me to the theory</button></div>
    <p class="ea-small" data-path-description>The chapters are ordered by prerequisite. Use the filters for shorter reading lists.</p>
    <label class="ea-small" for="chapter-search">Find a topic</label><input id="chapter-search" type="search" placeholder="Try identification, inference, or machine learning" data-chapter-search style="display:block;width:100%;max-width:38rem;padding:.8rem 1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);background:white;border-radius:3px;margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--ink);font-size:.85rem;" />
    <ol class="ea-chapters">{chapters.map(c=><li data-chapter-order={c.data.order} data-chapter-record data-search={`${c.data.title} ${c.data.description} ${c.data.question} ${c.data.part} ${chapterTopics[c.data.order]}`.toLowerCase()}><a href={`/econometrics/${c.id}/`}><span class="ea-number">{String(c.data.order).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><strong>{c.data.title}</strong><p>{c.data.description}</p><small>{chapterTopics[c.data.order]}</small><br/><small>{c.data.part} · about {c.data.minutes} min · <span data-chapter-status={c.id}>ready to read</span></small></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>)}</ol>
    <p hidden data-no-chapters>No chapter matches that search. Try a broader term.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="ea-dark"><div class="ea-shell ea-split"><div><p class="ea-kicker" style="color:#c2d2e6">For classrooms and working analysts</p><h2>Teaching materials</h2></div><div><p>The teaching guide includes a twelve-week schedule, a ninety-minute workshop, and a capstone on a training-program decision.</p><p><a href="/econometrics/teach/">Teaching plans, workshop, and capstone →</a></p><p><a href="/contact">Discuss training or quantitative research work →</a></p></div></div></section>
  <section class="ea-shell ea-band ea-split"><div><h2>Readings</h2><p>References include Hansen’s Econometrics and papers on difference-in-differences, instrumental variables, machine learning, and policy evaluation.</p><a href="/econometrics/readings/">References →</a></div><div><h3>About this edition</h3><p>The advanced chapters introduce topics that need further reading and problem sets for graduate study. This is a development edition.</p><a href="/econometrics/edition/">Edition notes →</a></div></section>
</Econometrics>
